  "additional": {
    "aboutAssay": "We tested this assay four times to validate this kit for measuring leptin in horse serum. Dilutions between 1:50 and 1:100 showed a trend toward acceptable linearity, while dilutions below 1:50 showed a clear matrix effect. At dilutions greater than 1:100, leptin was no longer reliably detected by the kit. Spike recovery was good (~80%) within the 1:50 to 1:100 dilution range.\n\nAlthough the results initially appeared promising within this narrow dilution range, the assay did not provide a sufficiently reliable working range for consistent measurement of leptin in horse serum. After four validation attempts, we decided to reject this kit for measuring leptin in equine serum.",
